\sectiontitle{Project Outcome/Deliverables (2 pts)}
\vspace{0.35cm}
\answerbox{%
\textbf{Phase 1}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=4mm,itemsep=2pt,topsep=2pt]
\item A working paper-setting pipeline that takes a teacher's CSV upload all the way through to an encrypted, compressed paper, with no manual steps in between.
\item CSV validation that catches a bad header or a bad row before it ever reaches the paper-generation logic, reporting the exact row, field, and problem back to the teacher.
\item Complete, documented C++ source for QuestionBank, TopicIndex, PaperGenerator, the Huffman compressor, and the key manager.
\item A question-bank upload screen with all three states (uploading, success, and error) wired to real backend output, not placeholder text.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Phase 2 (planned)}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=4mm,itemsep=2pt,topsep=2pt]
\item A working LCRS tree that broadcasts the encrypted paper down the server hierarchy using breadth-first traversal.
\item Per-node encryption via XOR key-chaining and AES-256, so every node's ciphertext is uniquely keyed by its position in the hierarchy.
\item An AVL-based node registry giving O(log n) lookup of any node's secret, key, and status.
\item A SHA-256 hash-chained transfer log, with a demonstration that tampering with any past entry is caught immediately.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Phase 3 (planned)}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=4mm,itemsep=2pt,topsep=2pt]
\item Time-locked decryption at the exam centre, so no readable paper exists before the scheduled exam time.
\item A multi-centre simulation covering several states, districts, and centres end to end.
\item A leak-tracing demonstration that takes a simulated leaked ciphertext and identifies its source node using only the AVL registry.
\end{itemize}}
\vspace{0.75cm}

\sectiontitle{Progress Overview (2 pts)}
\vspace{0.25cm}
\answerbox{%
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=4mm,itemsep=2pt,topsep=2pt]
\item Phase 1 is functionally complete: the full paper-setting pipeline (CSV upload, validation, QuestionBank/TopicIndex, PaperGenerator, Huffman compression, and encryption) is built and committed to the repository, along with the matching frontend upload screens.
\item The CSV checker code is complete; formal test logging (header-only, valid file, and row-error cases) is the one remaining item before Phase 1 can be marked fully validated.
